{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner complete Room-audit reading, 2026-10-04. All 853 lines of test-audit-room.md at immutable 2f83bf8c75c7fec706cd2310eeef5c986da0e2bb have now been read. Rechecked identity: 172,125 bytes, SHA-256 51344b187609033db2a62365dccf9379562a9df091930ffcb10ed80f218097d6. Earlier partial reading eedb09cf remains historical progress; its successor-mapping findings remain. The git/MCP/CLI/UI audit was read in full previously. Only lines 1-35 of the third audit have been read; its complete document and final audit judgment remain owed.\n\nStructural accounting is now independently checked. Filtering declaration rows by a path:line reference and a Retain/Rewrite/Remove decision, excluding fixture and aggregate tables, gives Room 565 rows (20/250/295), git/MCP/CLI/UI 697 (60/459/178), log/policy/client/checkers 617 (68/206/343), total 1,879 (148/915/816). There are no duplicate path:line references in that population. The four release-manifest script declarations outside packages/ are included. These match the reported aggregate dispositions; no correction to those totals is requested. This check does not establish discovery or expanded-case counts, completeness against the source tree, coverage of every useful invariant, or the claimed 2,053-case runtime gate. The population/runner distinction in 48583c65 is still owed.\n\nFour further precise successor requirements:\n\n1. Check results need the new job oracle, not the old monotone-evidence convention. Actual historical d691 body review-8faa2ef9.cases:329-404 sends two different signed check acts, first passing then failing on the same input, and asserts the failure causes no transition while the obligation remains met. This is not an exact duplicate-byte test. Its Rewrite reason 'late and duplicate results are history' loses that distinction. Specify the new case in terms of the exact selected job/result, scope incarnation, manifest/config/tree identity, and whether the second act is an update permitted by that job's definition, a new job, a superseded attempt or a refused conflicting result. R2's proposed requested/passed/failed states are non-final and permit explicit earlier selection; the new pending R3 states must be reconciled. Do not silently import the old 'any later failure cannot matter' rule. Conversely a lost admission reply can require delivering the retained result again; that must not run the checker again. Give the durable error/attention result its own witness, separate from a failed check and from a model's statement of success.\n\n2. Snapshot isolation needs both object reachability and consumer lifetime. Actual d691 snapshot-repos:127-211 checks that a newer filtered repository has no older snapshot commit or omitted blob, its commit has no parents, its advertised ref is exact, and each token reads its own repository but neither canonical nor another snapshot repository. It also checks shared reuse for the same snapshot commit, distinct per-job tokens, and a durable deletion duty after the last job. Rewrite that compact pair through the selected new interface. Checking only the current tree or commit digest does not prove omitted content cannot be fetched by object ID through history or leftover objects. Reuse must account for every still-live consumer and its exact token/duty; one job ending, a deadline or a new retry must not delete another consumer's repository or settle an old dispatched unknown. This does not require the obsolete preview/landing layout or a separate repository for each duplicate request. The observed old body is a fake-provider integration witness, not a live host guarantee.\n\n3. Safe sinks need a boundary witness in addition to the redactor's pure table. request-d268d249:151 is Remove because diag.cases proves redaction, while safe-errors:82,113 and request-d268d249:344 are Remove as replaced Room sinks/possible gaps. Actual d691 body at request-d268d249:151-171 injects provider text through the submit boundary and inspects both the client error and stored diagnosis for credential/query/userinfo leakage and a byte bound. A correct pure redactor alone cannot prove callers use it or that raw provider text never enters task/job/publication rows and views. Retire old routes and legacy error scrubs; assign one compact new O3 witness to the real new service-to-durable-record-to-browser/tool boundary, inspecting permitted safe metadata and protected credential custody separately. Avoid copying the same injected table into every app runner.\n\n4. Revocation/expiry assertions must match the declared observation and lifecycle bounds. Roster:165,321 and the rewritten hold/token rows currently read as immediate stopping of acts, reads or grants; review-aabda1ed:202-235 correctly identifies time passing during evaluation and with no new entry as separate cases. Specify the chosen observation-age and clock readings at commit, credential mint/dispatch and publication reservation. Pair before/at/after expiry and authority changes before/after observation with the actual bounded refusal/settlement behavior; reject a future observation/clock rollback as agreed. For streams and private exports, state their reauthorization/termination boundary. Revocation of device A with authorized B still active is a different result from loss of the controller's last active key. Ending a hold does not end responsibility, erase pending effects or prove a remote process stopped; already staged/reportable facts use the precise rule from the pending R3 revision. No test should imply stronger revocation immediacy or token/process cancellation than the accepted protocol actually provides.\n\nThe Room audit's final fifteen 'possible gaps' list is still out of date relative to its own delivered O1-O16 catalogue and the pending R1-R3 corrections. Give each applicable outcome an explicit retain-with-owner/rewrite/defer/remove decision and successor witness; old recorded-refusal caching, teams, old preview recomputation and legacy schema support do not return by default. The resulting pure/shared tables, actual DO admission/delivery cases, isolated Git/provider boundaries and whole browser/device journey remain distinct scopes. One shared fake must not become both implementation and the sole oracle.\n\nNo tests, installations, source edits, private diagnostic, live provider probe or deployment were performed. This is feedback under original R4 design-only request b18554a6 / promise f3c5d607 and direction d4e07064; it is neither design adoption nor source commissioning, and adds no Jam readiness gate. The 10x target covers the complete useful workflow and its setup/review costs, without restoring obsolete mechanisms.","body":{"execution":"none","head":"2f83bf8c75c7fec706cd2310eeef5c986da0e2bb","scope":"R4 complete Room-audit document reading; bounded historical source-body checks","verdict":"successor corrections requested; third audit still partial"}}